{"Serializer cross-field validation fails to enforce exactly one time field - both validate_timestamp and validate_age only run when their respective field is present, so a request with neither field passes validation despite the W3C spec requiring exactly one": 0.9362228512763977, "Early return on first invalid report silently skips remaining batch entries - the validation loop returns immediately on the first invalid report, so subsequent valid reports are never processed or metrically recorded": 0.9180200099945068, "Bulk delete lacks atomicity - file recordings are deleted before Kafka archive events are published; if publisher.flush() fails, recordings are permanently gone but replay metadata remains accessible and the job offset checkpoint may already be saved": 0.07299629598855972, "fetch_rows_matching_pattern() lacks error handling for Snuba query failures - if all retries are exhausted or an unexpected exception occurs, it will raise an unhandled exception that crashes the bulk delete task": 0.07352292537689209, "Non-SNUBA exceptions in fetch_rows_matching_pattern() (e.g., Organization lookup fails) have no catch handler": 0.116763174533844, "When fetch_rows_matching_pattern() crashes, job.offset is never updated and job status remains IN_PROGRESS indefinitely with no recovery mechanism": 0.18109802901744843, "TableWidgetVisualization renders empty data when feature flag is enabled - hardcoded empty data arrays instead of passing actual result.data and result.meta": 0.9949303269386292, "Test calls Visualize constructor with array argument instead of string - new Visualize([yAxis]) should be new Visualize(yAxis) after refactored constructor signature change": 0.40466389060020447, "BaseVisualize yAxes array conflicts with Visualize single-string yAxis refactor - toJSON() wraps the string in an array and getVisualizesFromLocation() expands it back via a nested loop, creating broken 1-to-N deserialization path": 0.41695636510849, "Null pointer dereference when data is undefined in useTraceItemAttributeKeys - data could be undefined if API returns error status after isFetching becomes false, but code doesn't check error before using data": 0.5844408273696899, "Visualize.replace() called with removed yAxes array parameter at lines 296 and 304 of aggregateColumnEditorModal.tsx - should use {yAxis: string} instead of {yAxes: [newYAxis]}": 0.06215643882751465, "toolbarVisualize.tsx constructs new Visualize([DEFAULT_VISUALIZATION]) with an array instead of string": 0.17836664617061615, "toolbarVisualize.tsx calls visualize.replace({yAxes: ...}) instead of {yAxis: string}": 0.020581459626555443, "toolbarVisualize.tsx accesses visualize.yAxes (now removed) at lines 54, 59, 66, 144, and 172": 0.037971917539834976, "Misleading field mapping in ReplayDeletionJobSerializer - obj.offset mapped to 'countDeleted' but offset is a pagination checkpoint during execution, only becoming actual count when job completes": 0.01855356991291046, "Potential null dereference in useFeedbackSummary - useApiQuery can return data as undefined even when isPending and isError are both false, but code accesses data.summary and data.numFeedbacksUsed without null guard": 0.9338683485984802, "ExploreParams expects visualizes to have yAxes array property but Visualize instances have yAxis: string (singular), causing potential runtime errors": 0.9099167585372925}